.TH CYAML_LIST_PUSH 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_list_push \- append a child to a list
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

ccol_retval_t cyaml_list_push(cyaml seq, cyaml child);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Append child to the CYAML_LIST node seq.  Ownership of child
transfers unconditionally: on success seq owns it, and on any failure
it is deep-freed by this function.  Do not free child afterwards
regardless of the return value.

child must not be seq itself, nor a node that already contains seq
somewhere in its own subtree.  This is not checked; creating such a
cycle makes a later cyaml_destroy(), cyaml_clone(), or
cyaml_serialize() call on the tree undefined behaviour.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
seq    CYAML_LIST target node.
child  Node to append.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success, ccol_invalid_args (if seq or child is NULL, or seq is
not a list), ccol_not_enough_memory, or ccol_container_full (the
list has reached its maximum representable element count; not
reachable in practice).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_list_get (3),
.BR cyaml_list_len (3),
.BR cyaml_create_list (3)
